  "prompt": "How much shade would the 18-story building proposed at 1550 Bedford Avenue in Crown Heights, Brooklyn add to the block across Eastern Parkway from it, between Franklin Avenue and Bedford Avenue? Use the Crown Heights dataset in the catalog: NYC's building footprints with their roof heights in metres, that block's outline and the site's lot, and the street centerlines with their roadway widths. Add the proposed building to the buildings as an edit a user can change on a map: its base to 135 feet on the lot, set back 30 feet from Eastern Parkway, and its upper floors to 185 feet, set back above the base, 10 feet from Eastern Parkway and Bedford Avenue and 15 feet from Union Street. Let the user choose to accumulate the shadow over one date, one month or the whole year, with a date picker and a month list. Cover the area with 3 metre ground cells and, on the GPU, cast sun rays from every cell every 10 minutes of every selected day, counting the minutes only the proposed building blocks the sun. Map the accumulated shadow in hours with the block highlighted, the proposed building in its own color and the other buildings and the streets around it, and show in a table the selection and the shade added on the block, the mean over its cells.",
