  "notes": "Three data loaders (buildings, Block 1259 and streets) and three Parameter nodes (the period, a date and a month). A Map Edits node adds the proposed building in two parts and feeds the map it is linked to by an interaction edge. Python nodes make the ground cells with the selection's days and hand the building's parts to an Autark compute step, a WGSL shader that accumulates each cell's minutes of the building's shadow; Python nodes then read the shadow per cell, keep the shaded cells for the map with its legend's whole-hour ends, make the map's extent and average the shade on Block 1259, which a Simple View shows. The Autark map draws the streets, the buildings, the shadow and the block."
